      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've made another report on this bug. It's happening again, and the gesture manager mirrors this. INFORMATION: This ONLY happens when putting buttons on avatars. \n\nExample: I created a charged attack system, if you hold a button through the entire charge animation, it plays a much stronger version of the attack. If you let go of the button early, or tap the button, it uses a less powerful version of said attack. \n\nThe problem: As of recently, ALL buttons I place on recently uploaded avatars are not functional. (within the last week) If I replace said buttons with toggles, they display, and function as intended. If I change them back to a button, they go back to being blank, with the name \"Button Text\" exactly as displayed in the screenshots posted by cubee_cb. I am using SDK 3.8.0, and this bug was present on version 3.7.6. This is how the animator is laid out.\n\nThe only solution I've found is to replace the button with a toggle.\n\nHow it SHOULD work: Pressing the button should set the boolean value to \"true\" until the user stops holding the button, in which case the value should return to \"false\". This was the basis on which I built this charged attack system on.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
